# ------------------------------
# mac-client layer (machine role)
# ------------------------------
# The personal Mac workstation: GUI apps, fonts, App Store apps, and the mobile
# build tooling the work on this box needs.
# Machine-role layer: pick this or hermes-server for a given box.
#
# The Flutter and Dart SDKs are not here. `config/mise/config.toml` pins
# `flutter`, which is the same reason FVM is gone: two version managers for one
# runtime means the version that wins is whichever shim PATH reaches first.
# What stays is the build tooling that sits on top of the SDK.
#
# This is a curated list, not a snapshot of one machine. An app earns a line
# here when the tracked configuration in this repo needs it or the setup would
# be wrong without it. Software installed by hand for a one-off, a client, or a
# hobby stays out, so `brew bundle` never becomes a way to reinstall everything
# that ever landed in /Applications.
#
# Install with: ./setup/layer.zsh mac-client   (after setup/install.zsh)

# Mobile Development
brew 'cocoapods'
brew 'fastlane'
brew 'firebase-cli'

# Mac App Store CLI (used by the `mas` block below)
brew 'mas'

# Reverse engineering — interactive GUI app. Pairs with the headless
# `brew 'ghidra', link: false` formula in the hermes-server layer.
cask 'ghidra'

# Casks
cask '1password'
cask 'android-studio'
cask 'claude'
cask 'cursor'
cask 'cyberduck'
cask 'dbeaver-community'
cask 'discord'
cask 'docker-desktop'
cask 'firefox'
cask 'google-chrome'
cask 'jordanbaird-ice'
cask 'karabiner-elements'
cask 'keepingyouawake'
cask 'licecap'
cask 'netron'
cask 'ngrok'
cask 'notion-calendar'
# The vault `zshenv` pins as OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH is read and written by Hermes'
# note-taking and llm-wiki skills. This is the app the human edits it in.
cask 'obsidian'
cask 'orbstack'
cask 'raycast'
cask 'slack'
cask 'ghostty'
# Declared here rather than installed by a `brew install --cask` line in a setup
# step, which is where it lived (`setup/install/99_toy.zsh`). A package no
# manifest names is a package `brew bundle` cannot reproduce and this repo
# cannot audit. Packet capture is a workstation activity; the headless server
# has no display to run the GUI on.
cask 'wireshark'

# Fonts
# Both families are named by config/ghostty/config: Monaspace Neon is the
# primary face, HackGen covers the Japanese codepoint ranges it maps out.
cask 'font-hack-nerd-font'
cask 'font-hackgen'
cask 'font-monaspace'

# Mas
if ENV['CI'] != 'true'
  mas 'Keynote', id: 409183694
  mas 'Kindle', id: 302584613
end

